<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Toghon Temür</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fled <a href="/years/1368">1368</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Toghon Temur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Toghon Temür was the last emperor of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a> to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. His reign was marked by factional conflict, natural disasters and widespread rebellion, including the Red Turban uprisings. In 1368, as Ming forces approached the capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dadu">Dadu</a>, he fled north to the Mongolian steppe, marking the end of Yuan rule in China.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/toghon-temur.jpg" alt="Toghon Temür" width="320" height="316" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 松照庵 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%85%83%E9%A0%86%E5%B8%9D%E5%A6%A5%E6%AD%A1%E5%B8%96%E6%9C%A8%E5%85%92_Emperor_Shun_of_Yuan_Toghon_Tem%C3%BCr.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
